                <pb facs="0058" n="48" sameAs="frus:frus1941v06/pg48"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/10554: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-05-02T14:00:00-03:00">May 2, 1941—2 p.m.</date><lb/>[Received
                        4:11 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>389. Department’s No. 250, April 29, 10 p.m. Nabuco says that he will instruct
                    forthwith the Brazilian Ambassador in Madrid as desired.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
